  Description: "The touch of undeath runs through your blood. Your family tree might
    contain powerful undead, like a vampire. Tradition divine Bloodline Skills Intimidation,
    Religion Sorcerous Gifts cantrip @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Void Warp],
    1st: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Harm], 2nd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.See
    the Unseen], 3rd: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Bind Undead], 4th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Talking
    Corpse], 5th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Invoke Spirits], 6th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Vampiric
    Exsanguination], 7th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Execute], 8th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Canticle
    of Everlasting Grief], 9th: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Wails of the
    Damned] Bloodline Spells initial: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Undeath's
    Blessing], advanced: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Drain Life], greater:
    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Grasping Grave] Blood Magic\u2014Stolen
    Life You can channel the necromantic energy in your blood. Either you gain temporary
    Hit Points equal to the spell's rank that last until the start of your next turn,
    or a target takes 1 void damage per spell rank (if the spell already deals initial
    void damage, combine this with the spell's initial damage before determining
    weaknesses and resistances)."
